elgium, targeting German columns that had advanced deep into Allied lines. Many pilots were airborne within minutes of the order. Forward air controllers guided strikes with growing precision, directing aircraft to roads choked with vehicles. German tanks and trucks, often stuck in traffic or short on fuel, were ideal targets. By the end of the day, hundreds of sorties had hit supply lines, bridges, and convoys. The Luftwaffe, already depleted, was unable to contest the skies. The sudden and overwhelming air response crippled the momentum of the German offensive and the tide began to turn. This rapid arrival of air power not only halted further German advances but helped encircle key enemy formations. The 23 December counterstrikes marked a turning point in the battle, proving how quickly Allied air forces could exploit a change in weather to devastating effect."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Homefront","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardDestroyed"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Class_Specific_Engineer_Socket_Crank_Sequence_2'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Class_Specific/War_UI_Class_Specific_Engineer_Socket_Crank_Sequence_2.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/USA/10_Homefront/T_swift_response.T_swift_response","SubPathString":""},"historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/SWIFT_RESPONSE.SWIFT_RESPONSE","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_swift_response_photo","SourceString":"P-47 Thunderbolt fighter bombers of the 365th Group taking off for a tactical support mission during the Battle of the Bulge, December 1944.","LocalizedString":"P-47 Thunderbolt fighter bombers of the 365th Group taking off for a tactical support mission during the Battle of the Bulge, December 1944."},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/BP_AttackOrder.BP_AttackOrder_C","SubPathString":"